WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.608 --> 00:00:17.874
"Way to go, Maggie!"

2
00:00:18.214 --> 00:00:18.875
Henry yelled.

3
00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:20.856
Cole let out a cheer too.

4
00:00:21.936 --> 00:00:23.557
Maggie grinned proudly as Ms.

5
00:00:23.597 --> 00:00:25.878
Wood attached the blue ribbon to her pony's bridle.

6
00:00:26.938 --> 00:00:28.659
Most of the other riders looked happy too.

7
00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:31.200
Only one rider looked unhappy.

8
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:32.921
That was Rebecca.

9
00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:34.121
She'd come in fourth.

10
00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:38.344
knew it!"

11
00:00:38.564 --> 00:00:41.606
she yelled, riding out of the ring and jumping down from her pony.

12
00:00:41.626 --> 00:00:44.568
"I would have won if I'd been riding Coco!"

13
00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:48.171
She flung her pony's reins away and kicked at the ground.

14
00:00:48.891 --> 00:00:51.913
Then she grabbed the white ribbon from the pony's bridle and stomped on it.

15
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:54.315
"Rebecca!" Ms.

16
00:00:54.355 --> 00:00:55.095
Wood exclaimed.

17
00:00:55.115 --> 00:00:57.677
"You should be ashamed of yourself!

18
00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.518
That's very poor sportsmanship."

19
00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:01.179
"I don't care!"

20
00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:02.020
Rebecca yelled.

21
00:01:02.772 --> 00:01:03.573
"It's not fair!

22
00:01:03.913 --> 00:01:05.194
I wanted to ride Coco today.

23
00:01:05.914 --> 00:01:07.815
This stupid pony made me lose!"

24
00:01:07.835 --> 00:01:09.876
"Don't say that!"

25
00:01:10.116 --> 00:01:11.157
another girl spoke up.

26
00:01:12.097 --> 00:01:13.798
"Red is a great pony too."

27
00:01:13.818 --> 00:01:16.120
"Yeah," Maggie agreed.

28
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.601
"I rode him once.

29
00:01:17.721 --> 00:01:18.561
He was awesome!

30
00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.202
Almost as good as Big Spot."

31
00:01:21.023 --> 00:01:21.903
"They're right, Rebecca."

32
00:01:22.143 --> 00:01:23.384
Ms. Wood sounded stern.

33
00:01:23.404 --> 00:01:26.646
"Now stop complaining and go take care of your pony.

34
00:01:27.506 --> 00:01:30.408
He did his best, and he deserves a nice grooming and some treats."

35
00:01:31.632 --> 00:01:32.953
A woman pushed through the crowd.

36
00:01:32.973 --> 00:01:37.017
"I think that's Rebecca's mother," Henry whispered to Cole.

37
00:01:38.038 --> 00:01:40.460
"Stop this tantrum right now and do as Ms.

38
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.300
Wood says!"

39
00:01:41.661 --> 00:01:42.621
Rebecca's mother said.

40
00:01:42.642 --> 00:01:45.864
"Or you won't get to take riding lessons anymore."

41
00:01:45.884 --> 00:01:48.667
"Fine!" Rebecca cried.

42
00:01:48.687 --> 00:01:51.429
"But it's not fair!"

43
00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:55.312
She stomped off toward the barn, dragging her pony behind her.

44
00:01:55.332 --> 00:01:58.235
"Wow. Did you see that?"

45
00:01:58.515 --> 00:01:59.536
Henry said to Cole.

46
00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.483
"Rebecca is obviously still mad about not getting to ride Coco."

47
00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:06.405
Cole just shrugged.

48
00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:09.988
"Yeah. She's probably the shirt thief, like you said."

49
00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:12.850
Henry rubbed his chin thoughtfully.

50
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.573
"She has a good motive.

51
00:02:16.974 --> 00:02:18.956
And she definitely could have done it.

52
00:02:19.736 --> 00:02:21.498
Now all we have to do is prove it."

53
00:02:21.518 --> 00:02:24.460
"That's not going to be easy," Cole said.

54
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.764
"If there were any witnesses, somebody would have said something by now.

55
00:02:29.644 --> 00:02:34.147
Plus, if Rebecca hid that shirt somewhere, it will be tough to prove that she was the one

56
00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:34.787
who stole it.

57
00:02:35.948 --> 00:02:39.429
Maybe we should just forget about this case and focus on selling lemonade."

58
00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.711
Henry frowned at his friend.

59
00:02:42.471 --> 00:02:44.172
Cole wasn't acting like himself today.

60
00:02:44.192 --> 00:02:48.394
"The Lemonade Detectives agreed to accept this case.

61
00:02:49.455 --> 00:02:51.876
That means we need to try to solve it!

62
00:02:52.837 --> 00:02:55.818
If you don't want to help, Maggie and I can do it without you."

63
00:02:57.299 --> 00:02:58.180
Cole frowned too.

64
00:02:58.976 --> 00:03:01.378
"I'm not saying I don't want to help," he said.

65
00:03:01.398 --> 00:03:05.441
"I'm just saying it's not going to be easy to prove anything.

66
00:03:06.402 --> 00:03:10.545
Besides, Daisy's family lives in that big, fancy house over on Elm Street.

67
00:03:11.426 --> 00:03:13.848
They have plenty of money to buy her another shirt.

68
00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:16.030
So what's the big deal?"

69
00:03:17.091 --> 00:03:19.713
Henry was surprised to hear Cole say something like that.

70
00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:22.195
"Stealing is wrong!"

71
00:03:22.415 --> 00:03:23.316
he reminded Cole.

72
00:03:24.316 --> 00:03:28.957
"If Rebecca stole Daisy's shirt, she should give it back to Daisy and apologize.

73
00:03:29.978 --> 00:03:33.038
And if she didn't do it, we should figure out who did."

74
00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:37.200
Just then he saw Rebecca come stomping out of the barn.

75
00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.501
"There's our suspect now," Henry told Cole.

76
00:03:41.341 --> 00:03:42.701
"Stay with the lemonade stand.

77
00:03:42.981 --> 00:03:43.721
I'll be right back."

78
00:03:45.362 --> 00:03:47.502
Henry hurried off without waiting for an answer.

79
00:03:48.423 --> 00:03:50.223
He caught up to Rebecca near the parking lot.

80
00:03:51.404 --> 00:03:52.724
"Hi, Rebecca," he said.

81
00:03:53.388 --> 00:03:54.289
"Can I talk to you?"

82
00:03:55.349 --> 00:03:57.211
"Sure, what do you want to talk about?"

83
00:03:57.371 --> 00:03:58.131
Rebecca asked.

84
00:03:59.072 --> 00:03:59.812
Henry shrugged.

85
00:03:59.832 --> 00:04:03.255
"I just wanted to congratulate you," he said.

86
00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:06.257
"I saw you win fourth place just now.

87
00:04:07.297 --> 00:04:11.320
That's pretty good, especially since you didn't get to ride your favorite pony."

88
00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.461
"Tell me about it!"

89
00:04:13.661 --> 00:04:14.482
Rebecca scowled.

90
00:04:14.502 --> 00:04:17.644
"I still can't believe Daisy stole Coco from me!

91
00:04:18.204 --> 00:04:19.485
It's totally unfair!"

92
00:04:19.505 --> 00:04:23.188
"Yeah," Henry said, pretending to go along with her.

93
00:04:24.384 --> 00:04:27.385
"So did you go visit Coco in her stall earlier?

94
00:04:28.266 --> 00:04:30.007
You know, before the show started?"

95
00:04:30.027 --> 00:04:32.748
"Huh?" Rebecca blinked at him.

96
00:04:32.768 --> 00:04:36.850
"Yeah, I stopped by and gave her a carrot when I first got here.

97
00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.471
Why?" "Just curious."

98
00:04:39.791 --> 00:04:40.851
Henry cleared his throat.

99
00:04:40.871 --> 00:04:45.773
"Was that before or after Daisy arrived at the show?"

100
00:04:45.793 --> 00:04:47.634
"How should I know?"

101
00:04:47.894 --> 00:04:48.575
Rebecca said.

102
00:04:48.595 --> 00:04:51.456
"Why are you asking all these questions, anyway?"

103
00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.862
"I, uh Henry tried to think of something to say.

104
00:04:56.923 --> 00:04:59.725
Lots of people in Belltown knew about The Lemonade Detectives.

105
00:05:00.726 --> 00:05:04.809
If Rebecca had stolen that shirt, Henry didn't want her to guess that he knew she'd done it.

106
00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.671
Otherwise it might be even harder to prove.

107
00:05:08.612 --> 00:05:11.093
Just then Henry heard a clatter of hooves behind him.

108
00:05:11.774 --> 00:05:14.816
Turning, he saw Maggie rushing over, still leading Big Spot.

109
00:05:14.836 --> 00:05:18.459
"I need to talk to you, Henry," Maggie said breathlessly.

110
00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:20.120
"In private."

111
00:05:21.072 --> 00:05:22.474
She yanked him away from Rebecca.

112
00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:27.801
is it?"

113
00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:28.722
Henry asked.

114
00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:30.805
Maggie spun to face him.

115
00:05:30.825 --> 00:05:33.228
"I just found Daisy's missing shirt!"
